            <ArticleTitle>Magnesium sulfate in the treatment of variant angina.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>46-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>41 episodes of anginal attacks were promptly terminated by a bolus of Mg sulfate administered intravenously in 15 patients with variant angina. Pretreatment with parenterally administered Mg sulfate in four of these patients prevented further attacks.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
